        'For each climate model, environmental changes are ratios of design-weighted paired-change numerators to valid area-time denominators, multiplied by the fixed region indicator. Three-model means average the model-specific domain ratios. Stratified ratio-influence variance uses all four original draws per stratum, retaining zero contributions from other regions and covariance across shared GCM draws. Domain MCSE is withheld below four sampled draws. GCM extrema and sample MCSE retain distinct meanings and exclude biological and fitting uncertainty. Supported weather–host domain terms retain the same four-corner validity mask and high-temperature exclusions as the continental decomposition; regional host offset is the ratio of ensemble component means.',
        'Spatial-sign summaries classify the paired mean change at each sampled cell for each GCM and SSP-period combination. The original design weights estimate the reference-area shares with a positive ensemble mean, positive or negative changes in all three GCMs, and mixed signs. Duplicate sampled cells retain both draw identities. Sign fractions describe the sampled model-response distribution; they do not establish observed affected hectares or probabilities of future disease. Three-GCM completeness and valid-year coverage accompany each displayed cell.'
