        'Public BASF and Corteva disease archives, NEX-GDDP-CMIP6v2 forcing, the GGCMI crop calendar, SPAM2020 harvested area and EEA environmental boundaries are identified by persistent dataset references. Source_Data.xlsx contains the numerical evidence for the retained figures and tables, including the full disease-labelled published crop-response contrasts, weather–host contributions, sampled-cell scenario changes, environmental-region statistics and spatial-sign area shares. Individual predictions, paired populations, forcing identities and source checksums accompany Software_and_Evidence.zip. [[Holst2022BASF|HolstDonner2022Corteva|NEXGDDPCmip6V2|GGCMIPhase32021|SPAM2020|EEA2016]]',
        'Raw whole-domain climate products and sampled-weather caches remain external. Their manifests identify source products, versions and checksums; publication regeneration uses the included completed numerical evidence. A forcing-based rerun additionally requires those climate inputs. Published crop-response transcriptions retain source tables, units, leaf scope, disease exposure and aggregate/fitted status. Unavailable plot observations, covariance and measured functional-area trajectories are not reconstructed.',
