        'For draw i, GCM m and region r, x contains the average paired change with invalid years set to zero, z the fraction of valid paired years, and I the fixed region indicator. The region estimate is ΣwIx/ΣwIz. Its influence is I(x−μz)/(ΣwIz). Stratum variance is the sum of squared stratum weights multiplied by within-stratum influence variance divided by four. Ensemble variance applies this rule to the mean GCM influence vector, preserving shared spatial-sample covariance. Region means are not recombined using external area totals because that would change the original sampling estimator.',
